  "body": "https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/system-state.html#cookies\r\n\r\n> The cookieEnabled attribute must return true if the user agent attempts to handle cookies according to HTTP State Management Mechanism, and false if it ignores cookie change requests\\. \\[COOKIES\\]\r\n\r\nIt may be good to explicitly list what behavior should be in cases where document.cookie would throw an exception (e.g. opaque origin). Present stable/beta[1] Chrome, Firefox, and Safari all seem to return true.\r\n\r\nCorresponding WPT testcase pull request:\r\nhttps://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/pull/18050\r\n\r\n[1] I broke it somewhat in Canary/Dev for a bit, but should be fixed shortly. ",
